                                        "sense_id": "0c265582-650d-34da-a8df-afd15043a55b",
                                        "entry_id": "56cb2148-26a3-311c-b328-3bc9b51eca21",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To stretch out, open out (a material etc.) so that it more fully covers a given area of space."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "104bf73c-55d6-4118-849a-0219d62c1558",
                                                "sense_id": "0c265582-650d-34da-a8df-afd15043a55b",
                                                "text": "He spread his newspaper on the table."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "543854ad-14ce-3fb3-87ce-7f17e74cb02d",
                                        "entry_id": "56cb2148-26a3-311c-b328-3bc9b51eca21",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To extend (individual rays, limbs etc.); to stretch out in varying or opposing directions. simple past and past participle of spread"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7a2f838e-faf1-4cb7-9f9d-d05d190d8f3b",
                                                "sense_id": "543854ad-14ce-3fb3-87ce-7f17e74cb02d",
                                                "text": "I spread my arms wide and welcomed him home."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c3676a15-cbed-3b57-a57c-a6670fb86828",
                                        "entry_id": "56cb2148-26a3-311c-b328-3bc9b51eca21",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To disperse, to scatter or distribute over a given area."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ae5faeec-5d92-4d05-887e-976cbdd526c3",
                                                "sense_id": "c3676a15-cbed-3b57-a57c-a6670fb86828",
                                                "text": "I spread the rice grains evenly over the floor."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "070f688e-c625-3732-8eb5-bed2bca71e23",
                                        "entry_id": "56cb2148-26a3-311c-b328-3bc9b51eca21",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To proliferate; to become more widely present, to be disseminated."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "68f78f21-d789-4b4b-b7d4-08bf07275d66",
                                                "sense_id": "070f688e-c625-3732-8eb5-bed2bca71e23",
                                                "text": "I placed my hands on his cheeks, and this time, I kissed him. “Don't worry, I'm not going to let anything spoil our day. It's just you and me.” A sad smile spread across his face, and I could tell he wanted to believe me, but didn't."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "99bca77e-0b8f-4d1b-91d3-73c0f871be2d",
                                                "sense_id": "070f688e-c625-3732-8eb5-bed2bca71e23",
                                                "text": "Whether modern, industrial man is less or more warlike than his hunter-gatherer ancestors is impossible to determine.[…]One thing that is true, though, is that murder rates have fallen over the centuries, as policing has spread and the routine carrying of weapons has diminished. Modern society may not have done anything about war. But peace is a lot more peaceful."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d3ce238a-59b2-463c-9441-2c02207179f4",
                                                "sense_id": "070f688e-c625-3732-8eb5-bed2bca71e23",
                                                "text": "As the Erzurum affair indicated, the janissaries in the provinces and in the capital city were in close touch, and thus the movements were quick to spread to Istanbul."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "68a100d6-3a73-3594-bcfb-7ebcd3bbcddf",
                                        "entry_id": "56cb2148-26a3-311c-b328-3bc9b51eca21",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To disseminate; to cause to proliferate, to make (something) widely known or present."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "82e5d8a2-54f2-4ddd-bb0a-a7a5bc2175ee",
                                                "sense_id": "68a100d6-3a73-3594-bcfb-7ebcd3bbcddf",
                                                "text": "The missionaries quickly spread their new message across the country."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e8830118-6044-3d86-86b0-f95c491b3c32",
                                        "entry_id": "56cb2148-26a3-311c-b328-3bc9b51eca21",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To take up a larger area or space; to expand, be extended."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "08bca109-a9e3-446e-bf42-0e1a8307e3e8",
                                                "sense_id": "e8830118-6044-3d86-86b0-f95c491b3c32",
                                                "text": "I dropped my glass; the water spread quickly over the tiled floor."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c7e0a5d5-b65c-35fd-b8c1-c6fcd7695073",
                                        "entry_id": "56cb2148-26a3-311c-b328-3bc9b51eca21",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To smear, to distribute in a thin layer."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "765c7bf0-8758-4ec5-99f7-d437e37b9012",
                                                "sense_id": "c7e0a5d5-b65c-35fd-b8c1-c6fcd7695073",
                                                "text": "She liked to spread butter on her toast while it was still hot."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "24cda66a-1f1a-35f1-810c-268f959ff538",
                                        "entry_id": "56cb2148-26a3-311c-b328-3bc9b51eca21",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To cover (something) with a thin layer of some substance, as of butter."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8aae2070-7123-45ac-b6eb-ee9ec5971744",
                                                "sense_id": "24cda66a-1f1a-35f1-810c-268f959ff538",
                                                "text": "He always spreads his toast with peanut butter and strawberry jam."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "188a0c6c-268f-326f-ba8f-db81d286c891",
                                        "entry_id": "56cb2148-26a3-311c-b328-3bc9b51eca21",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To prepare; to set and furnish with provisions."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4a9d9843-64a2-46c2-ba78-8b540ab476ce",
                                                "sense_id": "188a0c6c-268f-326f-ba8f-db81d286c891",
                                                "text": "to spread a table"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b3598621-74ec-4ca4-90e7-4902f3954688",
                                                "sense_id": "188a0c6c-268f-326f-ba8f-db81d286c891",
                                                "text": "And Enid brought sweet cakes to make them cheer, / And in her veil enfolded, manchet bread. / And then, because their hall must also serve / For kitchen, boil'd the flesh, and spread the board, / And stood behind, and waited on the three."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e05e7da6-fec2-32ed-8dae-2e9d068b5613",
                                        "entry_id": "56cb2148-26a3-311c-b328-3bc9b51eca21",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To open one’s legs, especially for sexual favours."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive",
                                            "slang"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "01795d19-3bb7-445b-b16a-26c777bf7a64",
                                                "sense_id": "e05e7da6-fec2-32ed-8dae-2e9d068b5613",
                                                "text": "This often sounds like the rap of a demented DJ: the way she moves has got to be good news, can't get loose till I feel the juice— suck and spread, bitch, yeah bounce for me baby."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3ada01c1-2861-4905-8c44-282b8f4ae75e",
                                                "sense_id": "e05e7da6-fec2-32ed-8dae-2e9d068b5613",
                                                "text": "Yes I wore a slinky red thing. Does that mean I should spread for you, your friends, your father, Mr Ed?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b4fb7a6e-87de-419a-9672-2e3ef46b8c18",
                                                "sense_id": "e05e7da6-fec2-32ed-8dae-2e9d068b5613",
                                                "text": "I don't want to move too fast, but / Can't resist your sexy ass / Just spread, spread for me; / (I can't, I can't wait to get you home)"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
